                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "Firstly, I would recommend purchasing this game on sale. It is not a bad game at all and it had even made me chuckle at some points. The voice acting and the game design is very good too. It certainly carries the vibe of 'classic' when it comes to horror. To be clear, it is not a scary game. There are horror elements but it mainly focus on setting the atmosphere like the book(I imagine). A bit spooky for its time~ I really did not expect the cultists to do that to each other... That was the only time I thought it was interesting and the craziness was short lived~ R.I.P that other guy.. \n\nAgain, it is not a bad story but you may find it a bit difficult to focus with the puzzles. It certainly carried the old era as you will miss things because they're faded into the background or you need to be pixel perfect. I had to use the guide because it will not let you put two and two together without Van Helsing. The most difficult puzzle was trying to unlock the shed with the code because Helsing needed to confirm he saw it. So much scratching at the wall!!! Some of the puzzles are not logic based either. I felt incredibly stupid playing this game. At least Van Helsing tells you that you're missing something before heading to the next part of the game, to save you coming back later but it can be insane. \n\nAlso Dracula is drunk on love. So drunk even the local drunkard is going 'what the fudge is wrong with you?'. Also clean up your damn castle! \n\nAs for Van Helsing... I didn't read the book but damn, he's a bit hardcore isn't he? The man really likes to use fire~",
